IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`
IMPORT `coa17-part21-ch1`

-- coa17-regulative.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Parts 21 and 21A: the duties that carry a time limit, as REGULATIVE
-- RULES (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... HENCE ... LEST ...). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. SOURCE and TARGET are as in
-- coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (a plain-text rendering, not the official text; the stable `l4` 1.6.110).
--
-- THE TWIN. Each duty here is also a decision function over facts in the module of its Part, and those are what the assertions
-- test: a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on the stable binary ("Trying to check equality on types that do not
-- support it", measured 2026-11-13), so a rule here is run with #TRACE in coa17-tests-regulative.l4 and its outcome is read from
-- the printed result, not counted by check.sh. coa17-check-traces.sh compares the printed outcomes with the expected ones.
-- THE CLOCK. WITHIN takes a bare number of days counted from entry, so each rule takes the day the period begins and works out
-- the number of days to the last day with the helpers of coa17-helpers.l4 (so "14 days beginning with the day" is 13, one
-- month beginning on 5 January is 30, two months after 5 January is 59): a #TRACE starts AT 0 on that day. The deadline is
-- inclusive (an act AT 13 is in time under WITHIN 13).
-- NOT MODELLED: "as soon as reasonably practicable" (s 790D(4)(a), 790E(4)(a), 790EA(4)(a)) and "as soon as practicable" (s 771(1)) have no day
-- count; the rules carry the hard limit and the decision functions carry the judgment as an input.

§ `Regulative rules: duties with a time limit`

-- src:9973 | (1) A company must, within two months after the allotment of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock, complete and have ready for delivery—
-- src:9974 | (a) the certificates of the shares allotted,
-- src:9975 | (b) the debentures allotted, or
-- src:9976 | (c) the certificates of the debenture stock allotted.
@ref s 769(1) Duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on allotment (src:9973-9976)
DECLARE `s 769(1) act under Part 21 or Part 21A` IS ONE OF
    `s 769(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents`
    `s 771(1)(a) register the transfer`
    `s 771(1)(b) give the transferee notice of refusal with its reasons`
    `s 776(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents after a transfer`
    `s 790D(4) give the notice to the person`
    `s 790E(4) give the person the notice of the change`
    `s 790EA(4) give the person the notice of ceasing`
    `s 790EB(2) notify the registrar of the failure to comply`
    `s 790EC(2) notify the registrar of the late compliance`
    `s 790ED(3) notify the registrar of the restrictions notice`
    `s 790EE(3) notify the registrar of the withdrawal notice`
    `s 790EF(3) notify the registrar of the court's order`
    `s 790G(2) inform the company of the status and give the required particulars`
    `s 790H(2) inform the company of the change and give the information`
    `s 790HA(2) inform the company that the person has ceased and of the date`
    `s 790LA(1) give the registrar a notice of the confirmed person`
    `s 790LC(1) give the registrar a notice of the unconfirmed person`
    `s 790LD(1) give the registrar a notice of the change`
    `s 790LE(1) give the registrar a notice of the pre-incorporation change`
    `s 790LF(1) give the registrar a notice that the person has ceased`
    `s 790LG(1) give the registrar a notice that the person named did not become a registrable person`
    `s 790LH(1) give the registrar a notice that it has no persons with significant control`
    `s 790LL(2) comply with the request`
    `s 790LM(2) deliver the statement that the person's identity is verified`
    `s 790LN(1) deliver the statement that the person's identity is verified`
    `s 790LO(2) deliver the statements about a relevant officer`
    `s 790LP(1) deliver the statements about a relevant officer`
    `s 782(2) order the company and any officer of it to make good the default`

@ref s 769(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery within two months after the allotment (src:9973)
GIVEN allotment IS A `s 769 allotment`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 769(1) act under Part 21 or Part 21A`
`s 769(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready (regulative rule)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 769(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` allotment
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 769(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents`
        WITHIN (Day (`s 769(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` allotment) MINUS Day (allotment's `s 769(1) the day of the allotment`))
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the documents were not complete and ready for delivery within two months after the allotment (s 769(1))"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:9993 | (1) When a transfer of shares in or debentures of a company has been lodged with the company, the company must either—
-- src:9994 | (a) register the transfer, or
-- src:9995 | (b) give the transferee notice of refusal to register the transfer, together with its reasons for the refusal,
-- src:9996 | as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date on which the transfer is lodged with it.
@ref s 771(1) Procedure on transfer being lodged (src:9993-9996)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 771 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 769(1) act under Part 21 or Part 21A`
`s 771(1) the company's duty to register the transfer or give notice of refusal (regulative rule)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 771(1) the company must register the transfer or give the transferee notice of refusal` transfer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        (   PARTY Company
            MUST `s 771(1)(a) register the transfer`
            WITHIN (Day (`s 771(1) the last day for registering the transfer or giving notice of refusal` transfer) MINUS Day (transfer's `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged`))
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the transfer was neither registered nor refused with reasons within two months after it was lodged (s 771(1))")
        ROR
        (   PARTY Company
            MUST `s 771(1)(b) give the transferee notice of refusal with its reasons`
            WITHIN (Day (`s 771(1) the last day for registering the transfer or giving notice of refusal` transfer) MINUS Day (transfer's `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged`))
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the transfer was neither registered nor refused with reasons within two months after it was lodged (s 771(1))")
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:10034 | (1) A company must, within two months after the date on which a transfer of any of its shares, debentures or debenture stock is lodged with the company, complete and have ready for delivery—
-- src:10035 | (a) the certificates of the shares transferred,
-- src:10036 | (b) the debentures transferred, or
-- src:10037 | (c) the certificates of the debenture stock transferred.
@ref s 776(1) Duty of company as to issue of certificates etc on transfer (src:10034-10037)
GIVEN transfer IS A `s 776 lodged transfer`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 769(1) act under Part 21 or Part 21A`
`s 776(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready after a transfer (regulative rule)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 776(1) the company must complete and have ready for delivery the documents` transfer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY Company
        MUST `s 776(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents after a transfer`
        WITHIN (Day (`s 776(1) the last day for completing the documents and having them ready for delivery` transfer) MINUS Day (`s 776(4) the day from which the period of two months runs` transfer))
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the documents were not complete and ready for delivery within two months after the transfer was lodged (s 776(1))"
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- src:10255 | (4) The company must give the notice—
-- src:10256 | (a) as soon as reasonably practicable after the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under this section, and
-- src:10257 | (b) in any event before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company becomes so subject.
@ref s 790D(4) The company must give the notice as soon as reasonably practicable and in any event before the end of the period of 14 days (src:10255-10257)
GIVEN `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under section 790D` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 769(1) act under Part 21 or Part 21A`
`s 790D(4) the duty to act within the period (regulative rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 790D(4) give the notice to the person`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under section 790D`) MINUS Day `the day on which the company becomes subject to the duty to give a notice under section 790D`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the notice was not given before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company became subject to the duty (s 790D(4)(b))"

