-- src:10460 | (3) A notice under subsection (1) must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation as mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 790LA(3) within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation (src:10460)
GIVEN `the day on which the company had confirmation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 769(1) act under Part 21 or Part 21A`
`s 790LA(3) the duty to act within the period (regulative rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 790LA(1) give the registrar a notice of the confirmed person`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the company had confirmation`) MINUS Day `the day on which the company had confirmation`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the registrar was not notified within 14 days beginning with the day of confirmation (s 790LA(3))"

